{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_54","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -lc \"sed -n '1,260p' PR_COMMENTS.md\"","aggregated_output":"Updated `MONDO:1060138` (`GRIN-related complex neurodevelopmental disorder`) by adding literature-backed synonyms and a tracker link to issue #9930.\n\nChanges made:\n- Added `GRIN-related neurodevelopmental disorder` as an `EXACT` synonym, supported by `PMID:36619673`.\n- Added `GRIN-related encephalopathy` as a `RELATED` synonym, supported by `doi:10.1093/brain/awae041`.\n- Added `grinpathies` as a `RELATED` synonym, supported by `PMID:34884460`.\n- Added `IAO:0000233 \"https://github.com/monarch-initiative/mondo/issues/9930\"` to link the term back to this request.\n\nRationale:\n- The requested umbrella labels are supported in the recent GRIN literature, but I did not add `GRIN-related complex neurodevelopmental disorder` as a synonym because it is already the primary label.\n- I used `grinpathies` instead of `GRINopathies` because the verifiable published usage I found uses `grinpathies`/`the so-called grinpathies` rather than the capitalized spelling.\n- I kept `GRIN-related encephalopathy` as `RELATED` rather than `EXACT`, because it is used in the literature as an umbrella label but is slightly less precise than the MONDO preferred name.\n\nChecks completed:\n- Reviewed the imported issue context in `__issue_context__.json`.\n- Verified current MONDO content for `MONDO:1060138` and nearby GRIN-related terms.\n- Verified synonym usage against the cited literature / publisher pages.\n- Ran ODK normalization with `make NORM` and replaced `src/ontology/mondo-edit.obo` with the normalized output.\n- Ran `robot convert --catalog src/ontology/catalog-v001.xml -i src/ontology/mondo-edit.obo -f obo -o mondo-edit.TMP.obo` successfully as a syntax check.\n\nLocal commit:\n- `f8c259c` `Add GRIN-related disorder synonyms`\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
